{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"8cebb687e50b3c70693bcc2ba704cab68c98d5e829a2869d75860b4b8b1c97d4","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI drift gate for docker-compose external volume provisioning","key_entities":["infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","infra/scripts/config-check.sh","make config-check","SITE_SUBDIRS","gerrit_reviewbot_tickets","--print-volumes"],"problem_keywords":["external volume","docker-compose","provisioning","drift detection","configuration validation","ci gate"],"propositions":["Every external volume declared in docker-compose.yml must be provisioned by compose-up.sh; undeclared external volumes cause compose-up to fail with 'external volume not found'.","compose-up.sh must expose a --print-volumes mode that outputs the derived external volume names deterministically and side-effect-free, for consumption by config-check.sh check 5.","config-check.sh check 5 must extract external volumes from docker-compose.yml via yaml.safe_load and compare against the output of compose-up.sh --print-volumes, failing loudly if the script exits non-zero or returns empty.","An embedded self-test must verify that a synthetic docker-compose snippet with an unprovisioned external volume (gerrit_notprovisioned) is detected by check 5, exiting non-zero with the volume name and compose-up.sh mentioned.","A second embedded self-test must verify that enumeration failure (e.g., missing compose-up.sh script) is reported as 'could not enumerate provisioned volumes' rather than silently passing on an empty set."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822788763813185,"uuid":"037d38a0-797b-4311-b9ea-0764c60490c5"}